# Casbin seed files (`casbin_*`)

If the user mentions a `casbin_*` prefix (e.g. `casbin_trip`, `casbin_payment`), treat that as a request to extend Casbin seed data in `backend/auth`.

## Do

- Update policy/grouping definitions in [backend/auth/script/casbin_seed.go](backend/auth/script/casbin_seed.go)
- Keep JSON in sync:
  - [backend/auth/database/seeders/json/casbin_policies.json](backend/auth/database/seeders/json/casbin_policies.json) — `p, <role>, <resource>, <create|read|update|delete>`
  - [backend/auth/database/seeders/json/casbin_grouping.json](backend/auth/database/seeders/json/casbin_grouping.json) — `g, <email>, <role>`
- Keep the CLI as `go run cmd/main.go --script:casbin_seed` (no extra flags)

## Policy shape

```
g, <user_email>, <customer|driver|admin>
p, <role>, <user|trip|payment|...>, <create|read|update|delete>
```
